// Kusto Query Language (KQL) - Storage Diagnostic Error Alert Query
//
// What this does:
//   Looks through the diagnostic logs collected for an Azure Storage Account (StorageBlobLogs)
//   and pulls out any requests that came back with a client or server error
//   (HTTP Status Code 400 or above) — things like Authorization Failures (403),
//   missing resources (404), or backend Server Errors (5xx).
//
// How the alert fires:
//   This query is meant to run on a 5-minute evaluation schedule. If the number of
//   failed transactions found in that window comes out Greater Than 5, the alert triggers.
StorageBlobLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| where StatusCode >= 400
| project TimeGenerated, AccountName, OperationName, StatusCode, StatusText, Uri, CallerIpAddress
| summarize ErrorCount = count() by AccountName, OperationName, StatusCode
| where ErrorCount > 5
| order by ErrorCount desc
